Description: 2k executable graphics by Suricrasia Online, released in 2020
 Storage Room is a 2 kilobyte executable graphics ("exegfx") for Linux by
 blackle of Suricrasia Online, ranked 3rd in the 4k procedural graphics
 competition at NOVA 2020. A GLSL path tracer renders, line by line, a
 single still image of a room full of glossy cubes.
 .
 It needs OpenGL 4.3 and renders a 1920x1080 image: the screen must be at
 least 1920 pixels wide. The SAMPLES environment variable sets the number
 of samples per pixel (300 by default).
 .
 This package is built from the sources, with the standard C library
 start-up code, instead of the size-optimised packed binary.
